 1], ["wm_noticeboard", 27, 45, "hgdpc_text", 1], ["hgdpc_post5", 30, 42, "hgdpc_text", 1], ["wm_noticeboard", 121, 15, "hgdpc_text", 1], ["hgdpc_post6", 123, 13, "hgdpc_text", 1], ["wm_noticeboard", 143, 27, "hgdpc_text", 1], ["hgdpc_post7", 145, 25, "hgdpc_text", 1], ["noticeboard", 41, 95, "hgdpc_text", 0.9], ["noticeboard", 30, 53, "hgdpc_text", 0.9], ["noticeboard", 120, 20, "hgdpc_text", 0.9], ["noticeboard", 148, 31, "hgdpc_text", 0.9], ["noticeboard", 76, 27, "hgdpc_text", 0.9], ["noticeboard", 174, 37, "hgdpc_text", 0.9], ["noticeboard", 12, 72, "hgdpc_text", 0.9], ["noticeboard", 178, 94, "hgdpc_text", 0.9], ["noticeboard", 17, 15, "hgdpc_text", 0.9], ["noticeboard", 46, 66, "hgdpc_text", 0.9]], "notes": ["0: Someone has scratched into the wall: I WALKED PAST THE SAME TREE FOUR TIMES. IT WAS A DIFF", "1: Chalked on the wall: The hedge maze is the easy part. Do not get cocky.", "2: A neat note: If you are reading this, you are lost. So was I. Turn left. No, the other lef", "3: Scratched small: There is a shortcut here. I walked into the wall to find it, and I was ri", "4: Written in charcoal: The slug is not slow. The slug is patient. There is a difference.", "5: A child's drawing of a worm, with a sign: DO NOT FEED. Underneath, someone has added: TOO ", "6: Carved deep: A KEY IS USED UP IN THE LOCK. SAVE THEM FOR THE GOOD DOORS.", "7: Chalked: Gem doors are worth the trouble. The treasure behind them is better than anything", "8: Scratched: The signs mean what they say. I have stood under one and watched a worm go by t", "9: A note pinned to the wall: LOST: one lantern, brass, very dear to me. If found, please do ", "10: Chalked: Four towns is a good walk. Eight towns is a good life.", "11: Carved: THE HONEYCOMB WALLS ARE WARM. THE SHELL WALLS ARE COLD. THE SANDSTONE WALLS HAVE S", "12: Scribbled: I came for the treasure and stayed for the soup. Ask in the towns.", "13: Scratched: Dead ends are not always dead. Press on the wall at the end, and press on the w", "14: Written small: The ponds are shallow and the fish are not real. Do not ask me how I know.", "15: Chalked on the stone: HEDGEFOOT IS THIS WAY. NO. THAT WAY. I AM NOT SURE ANY MORE.", "16: A note: Whoever keeps moving the walls, please stop.", "17: Carved: I found a gold key in a vault and a gold door two hours later. I have never been s", "18: Chalked: The warden at the top is not as clever as he looks. He is bigger than he looks, t", "19: Scratched: There are people living in the maze who have never seen the sky. They are very ", "20: A scrap of cloth nailed up: The Hollowed Warden was a gardener once. We do not talk about ", "21: Written in a neat hand: Rest in the safe places. Fight in the dangerous ones. Never confus", "22: Scratched: Blue door, blue key. Red door, red key. Gem door, gem. Nobody has ever been thi", "23: Chalked: I counted the steps from the start to the top. Then the maze changed my mind.", "24: Carved: Every maze has a middle. This one has several, and none of them is the middle.", "25: A note: If the lamp goes out, stand still. If the lamp goes out and something breathes, ru", "26: Scratched: The spiders are the worst. They are also, I am told, delicious. I have not test", "27: Chalked: Atriums are full of trees and quiet. Quiet is good. Trees are better. Ponds are b", "28: A child's writing: MY MOTHER SAYS NOT TO GO PAST THE SIGNS. I AM ON THE SAFE SIDE. I CAN S", "29: Carved by a careful hand: The Gilded Quarter is the richest and the most dangerous. They a", "30: Scratched: Something large went past here in the night, and it did not say good morning.", "31: Chalked: The Blue Quarter is quiet. Too quiet. I have gone back.", "32: A note: To whoever finds my gem: it was a gift. Please do not use it on a door. Marry some", "33: Written small: The mosaic was beautiful once. Then the dark came and the tiles began to fa", "34: Scratched: There are twelve people in the maze who will give you a task. I have done two. ", "35: Chalked: Every shop is better than the last, but the last is dearer. Choose wisely.", "36: Carved: The hollow slugs came up through the floor at the same time as the dark. Make of t", "37: A note: Do not trust a corridor that is too straight. Nobody built one."], "noteUse": [[0, 175, 25, 7], [2, 17, 17, 5], [5, 159, 69, 4], [6, 161, 48, 7], [8, 63, 61, 4], [10, 197, 97, 4], [11, 138, 69, 4], [13, 195, 34, 7], [15, 129, 9, 6], [16, 77, 37, 6], [17, 153, 24, 7], [19, 133, 49, 6], [23, 17, 63, 5], [24, 176, 41, 7], [26, 85, 68, 4], [28, 131, 33, 6], [30, 115, 26, 6], [31, 24, 95, 4], [38, 178, 61, 7], [40, 49, 56, 5]], "spots": [[3, 100, 12, true], [3, 42, 90, false], [3, 82, 56, false], [3, 58, 77, false], [3, 12, 101, false], [3, 143, 28, false], [3, 121, 16, false], [3, 28, 45, false], [2, 172, 35, false], [2, 178, 92, false], [2, 182, 17, false], [2, 75, 25, false], [2, 161, 43, false], [2, 191, 64, false], [2, 60, 42, false], [2, 147, 59, false], [2, 161, 21, false], [2, 15, 31, false], [2, 24, 76, false], [2, 128, 80, false], [2, 165, 60, false], [2, 177, 76, false], [2, 32, 29, false], [2, 15, 11, false], [2, 42, 48, false], [1, 75, 76, false], [1, 9, 81, false], [1, 50, 16, false], [1, 137, 59, false], [1, 112, 33, false], [1, 140, 10, false], [1, 14, 70, false], [1, 119, 27, false], [1, 188, 33, false], [1, 80, 14, false], [1, 17, 88, false], [1, 32, 81, false], [1, 41, 8, false], [1, 46, 63, false], [1, 190, 81, false], [1, 143, 47, false], [1, 49, 29, false], [1, 39, 19, false], [1, 176, 65, false], [1, 28, 65, false], [1, 89, 26, false], [1, 30, 11, false], [1, 89, 36, false], [1, 15, 50, false], [1, 62, 27, false], [1, 37, 62, false], [1, 39, 75, false]], "bioCount": [[4, 3901], [5, 3050], [6, 2058], [7, 2969]], "enemiesNearGiver": [], "lampsNearGiver": [["hgd_q9", 75, 25, "hgt_lamppost", 75, 24], ["hgd_q11", 14, 70, "hgtb_fishbeetle", 13, 70], ["hgd_q11", 14, 70, "wm_bookshelf", 14, 69], ["hgd_rest0", 178, 92, "yar_tent", 178, 91], ["hgd_rest2", 15, 11, "wm_lantern_gol